Project 4: Functions and Loops (10/06/2025)
Introduction
The goal of this project is to learn how to conduct mathematical calculations, create functions, utilize loops, and timing functions while continuing our practice of implementing our code into a physical electronic component. By passing a range of values through a mathematical function and displaying the input and output values, I was able to practice writing code that communicates information to the user while gaining experience using functions and loops to ease the process of what would otherwise be tedious work. This project continued increasing my knowledge of embedded systems applications, where displaying information that gets passed through complex functions reliably is fundamental.
Materials and Components
- Breadboard
- Raspberry PICO board
- LCD screen
- Circuit wires
Circuit Setup and Schematic

MicroPython Code
The following code is reproduced from the project report.
#Importing the LCD library, math functions, and time
from lcd1602 import LCD
import utime, math

#Setting my start value
x = -4.5

#Displaying the expression and range
lcd = LCD()
string = f"  Expression 4\n"
lcd.message(string)
utime.sleep(2)
lcd.clear()
string = f"   y = (x^3)*\n ((sin(x/3))/8)"
lcd.message(string)
utime.sleep(2)
lcd.clear()
string = f"  Minimum:-4.5\n  Maximum: 0.5"
lcd.message(string)
utime.sleep(2)
lcd.clear()

#Solving for the y values and displaying the input and output
while x <= 0.5:
y = (x**3)*((math.sin(x/3))/8)
string = f"    x:{x:.1f}\n"
lcd.message(string)
string = f"    y:{y:.1f}"
lcd.message(string)
utime.sleep(2)
lcd.clear()
x += 0.1
